shop.introToPhet.findSimulationsThatAreRelevant",s="virtualWorkshop.introToPhet.reflectOnActiveLearningFor",l="virtualWorkshop.introToPhet.embedSimulationsInYourTeaching",c="virtualWorkshop.introToPhet.twoHours",u="virtualWorkshop.introToPhet.whatShouldStudentsLearnIn",m="virtualWorkshop.introToPhet.whatDoesItReallyMean",d="virtualWorkshop.introToPhet.whichSkillsAndAttitudesShould",p="virtualWorkshop.introToPhet.isTheWayYouCurrently",h="virtualWorkshop.introToPhet.asABestPracticeEducational",g="virtualWorkshop.introToPhet.phETsGoalsForStudentAnd",y="virtualWorkshop.introToPhet.ifYouAreNotFamiliar",f="virtualWorkshop.introToPhet.letsStartWithABrief",b="virtualWorkshop.introToPhet.letsDiscussHowToFind",v="virtualWorkshop.introToPhet.thePhEtTeamWorksTo",S="virtualWorkshop.introToPhet.nowThatYouHaveLearned",P="virtualWorkshop.introToPhet.takeAMomentToGet",k="virtualWorkshop.introToPhet.whatStrategiesCouldYouInclude",E="virtualWorkshop.introToPhet.howCanYouCreateAn",w="virtualWorkshop.introToPhet.customizeScreensYouCanModify",T="virtualWorkshop.introToPhet.congratulationsYouHaveCompletedThe",O="virtualWorkshop.introToPhet.letsMakeAPlanFor",I="virtualWorkshop.introToPhet.ifYouAreTakingThis",C="virtualWorkshop.introToPhet.nowThatYouKnowHow",L="virtualWorkshop.introToPhet.getTheMostOutOf",j="virtualWorkshop.introToPhet.workThroughTheCourseContent",x="virtualWorkshop.introToPhet.whenWatchingVideosClickOn",A="virtualWorkshop.introToPhet.downloadReadAnnotateAndSave",N="virtualWorkshop.introToPhet.engageAuthenticallyWithAllOf",D="virtualWorkshop.introToPhet.takeTimeToEngageIn",M="virtualWorkshop.introToPhet.beforeWeEngageWithPhEt",R="virtualWorkshop.introToPhet.learningGoalsSubTitle",F="virtualWorkshop.introToPhet.activeLearningWithPhet",_="virtualWorkshop.introToPhet.selectingPhEtSimsTemplate",B="virtualWorkshop.introToPhet.wholeClassStrategiesLearnStrategies",W="virtualWorkshop.introToPhet.reflectOnTheFollowing",K={[i]:"Introduction to PhET",[o]:"In this virtual workshop, you will learn how to access and share PhET simulations with your students, and explore the features that make PhET sims a powerful tool for science and mathematics teachers.",[r]:"Learn what makes PhET simulations unique.",[a]:"Find simulations that are relevant to your classes.",[s]:"Reflect on Active Learning for effectively integrating simulations into your teaching.",[l]:"Embed simulations in your teaching materials and share them with others.",[c]:"2 hours",[u]:"What should students learn in a mathematics or science class?",[m]:"What does it really mean to learn a concept?",[d]:"Which skills and attitudes should be encouraged in a mathematics or science class?",[p]:"Is the way you currently teach the most effective approach to help your students learn? Why?",[h]:"As a best practice, educational activities should begin with identifying the learning goals for your students. In that respect, the PhET project and its sims are no exception. We invite you to get familiar with the following document that presents PhET’s suggested learning goals for you and your students.",[g]:"PhET’s Goals for Student and Teachers",[y]:"If you are not familiar with PhET, this section will provide an overview of the history and goals of the PhET project.",[f]:"Let’s start with a brief video introduction to the PhET project from the perspective of teachers, students, and members of the PhET team. (Note: Although the video refers only to PhET’s science sims, PhET sims address a range of topics from mathematics and science.)",[b]:"Let’s discuss how to find and select the best sim for your class. The next video gives you a tour of the PhET website and describes how to access the multitude of resources available on the site.",[v]:"The PhET team works to make sims accessible for all students. Check the <a {{link1}}>accessible features</a> that are available on some of our sims, and learn more about <a {{link2}}>our commitment to accessibility</a>.",[S]:"Now that you have learned a bit about PhET, it’s time to have some fun with our sims! The purpose of this activity is to explore the sims, notice features you can discover within the sim, and identify questions you have about the sims or their features. Try out 4-5 different mathematics or science sims and write down your thoughts.",[P]:"Take a moment to get familiar with Active Learning, its characteristics, and how to connect this approach with PhET sims.",[k]:"What strategies could you include in your class to move towards a more active class with sims?",[E]:"How can you create an environment where students are motivated and engaged?",[w]:"<span {{class}}>Customize Screens:</span> You can modify the URL of a sim to customize the number and order of screens within the PhET sim.",[T]:"Congratulations! You have completed the Intro to PhET Simulations workshop.",[O]:"Let’s make a plan for which sims you want to use in your classroom. Review the instructions for the activity in the document below.",[I]:"If you are taking this course independently, we recommend that you complete the following activity and save it to your computer. (Should you later decide to enroll in a facilitated version of this course, you can then submit these assignments to earn a certificate).",[C]:"Now that you know how to navigate the PhET website to find sims and teacher resources, continue your learning journey with one of our other workshops:",[L]:"Get the most out of this workshop! We make the following recommendations:",[j]:"Work through the course content at your own pace. However, we encourage you to do the workshop alongside a colleague to learn and share with each other.",[x]:"When watching videos, click on the settings icon to adjust playback speed and subtitles (in English or other languages).",[A]:"Download, read, annotate, and save documents for future reference.",[N]:"Engage authentically with all of the course activities. All example sim-centered activities provided by PhET have a link to an editable Google Doc in their footers.",[D]:"Take time to engage in the discussions. If you are not working with a colleague, take time to record your self-reflections.",[M]:"Before we engage with PhET and its teaching strategies, it is important to think about what you want your students to achieve when using simulations (sims).",[R]:"Learning Goals",[F]:"Active Learning with PhET",[_]:"Selecting PhET Sims Template ",[B]:"<a {{link}}>Whole-Class Strategies:</a> Learn strategies to use PhET with whole-class activities.",[W]:"Reflect on the following:"}}},math:{"VirtualWorkshopMath.jsx":function(e,t,n){var i,o,r;let a,s,l,c,u,m;n.export({VirtualWorkshopMath:()=>d}),n.link("prop-types",{default(e){a=e}},0),n.link("react",{default(e){s=e}},1),n.link("../common/constants.ts",{MATH(e){l=e}},2),n.link("../common/VirtualWorkshop.jsx",{VirtualWorkshop(e){c=e}},3),n.link("./mathData.jsx",{MATH_DATA(e){u=e}},4),n.link("./mathStrings.ts",{MATH_FALLBACK_STRINGS(e){m=e}},5);class d extends(i=s.Component){render(){return s.createElement(c,{section:this.props.section,workshopType:l,title:u.title,sections:u.sections,strings:m})}constructor(e){super(e)}}o="propTypes",r={section:a.string},o in d?Object.defineProperty(d,o,{value:r,enumerable:!0,configurable:!0,writable:!0}):d[o]=r},"mathData.jsx":function(e,t,n){let i,o,r,a,s,l,c,u,m,d,p,h,g,y,f,b,v,S,P,k,E,w,T,O,I,C,L,j,x,A,N,D,M,R,F,_,B,W,K,U,H,q,G,Y,$,z,V,Q,J,Z,X,ee,et,en,ei,eo,er,ea,es,el,ec,eu,em,ed,ep,eh,eg,ey,ef,eb,ev,eS,eP,ek,eE,ew,eT,eO,eI,eC,eL,ej,ex,eA,eN,eD,eM,eR,eF,e_,eB,eW,eK,eU,eH,eq,eG,eY,e$,ez,eV,eQ,eJ,eZ,eX,e1,e0,e2,e3,e5,e4,e7,e6,e9,e8,te,tt,tn,ti,to,tr,ta,ts,tl,tc,tu,tm,td,tp,th,tg,ty,tf,tb,tv,tS,tP,tk,tE,tw,tT,tO,tI,tC,tL,tj,tx,tA,tN,tD,tM,tR;n.export({MATH_DATA:()=>tF},!0),n.link("website-common/geo",{ENGLISH_LOCALE(e){i=e}},0),n.link("../../../../../../api/data/constants.ts",{STATIC_MOUNT_PATH(e){o=e}},1),n.link("../../../activities/contribute-edit/CreateActivityPage.tsx",{CreateActivityPage(e){r=e}},2),n.link("../common/constants.ts",{ACT